# Cloudflare direct API token setup. Keep credentials out of Telegram messages.
@origin = http://localhost:3000
@workspace = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@session = replace-with-your-session
@csrf = replace-with-your-csrf-token

### Save the token, initially disabled (use current revision for existing settings)
# Token resource restrictions should match the intended account and domains.
# Prefer account API tokens: https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/api-tokens
# User API tokens also work; User Memberships Read enables their account discovery.
# Account Settings Read verifies an account. Use manual IDs if discovery is unavailable.
# Add Zone Read, DNS Read and Pages Read as needed; traffic needs zone Analytics Read.
# Other products need their Read permissions. Reviewed writes need DNS Edit,
# Cache Purge, Zone Settings Edit or Workers Routes Edit as appropriate.
PUT {{origin}}/api/admin/workspaces/{{workspace}}/plugins/cloudflare
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "revision": 0,
  "settings": { "enabled": false, "authMethod": "api_token", "accountId": "", "zoneIds": [] },
  "apiToken": "replace-with-your-scoped-cloudflare-token"
}

### Discover accounts; follow page/hasMore if needed
POST {{origin}}/api/admin/workspaces/{{workspace}}/plugins/cloudflare/resources
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "revision": 1, "resource": "accounts", "page": 1 }

### Discover domains in an account returned above; grants no tool scope
POST {{origin}}/api/admin/workspaces/{{workspace}}/plugins/cloudflare/resources
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "revision": 1, "resource": "zones", "accountId": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", "page": 1 }

### Verify and save the explicit selection; omit domains for account resources only
# If the token cannot discover accounts, manually supply IDs and omit verifyResources.
# Manual saves do not verify provider permissions; tools still enforce their scope.
PUT {{origin}}/api/admin/workspaces/{{workspace}}/plugins/cloudflare
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "revision": 1,
  "settings": {
    "enabled": true,
    "authMethod": "api_token",
    "accountId": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
    "zoneIds": ["bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb"]
  },
  "verifyResources": true
}

### Read the saved summary (no token or ciphertext)
GET {{origin}}/api/admin/workspaces/{{workspace}}/plugins/cloudflare
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}

# Private Telegram journey after configuration:
# 1. "Show the Cloudflare domains available in this workspace."
# 2. "List DNS records for example.com. Fetch the next page if needed."
# 3. "Show the latest Pages deployments for my-site."
# 4. Owner/admin: "Create an A record for www.example.com pointing to
#    192.0.2.10, automatic TTL, proxy disabled."
#    Inspect the complete proposal, then press its actor-bound Approve button.
# 5. Owner/admin: "Purge https://www.example.com/index.html from the cache."
#    Inspect and approve the new exact request separately.
# 6. "Summarize example.com traffic for the last seven complete UTC days, then by country."
#    Tool: {"resource":"zone_analytics","zoneId":"bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb"}
#    Add since/until (YYYY-MM-DD, max 31 days), dimension country/status/content/browser.
# 7. "List Worker scripts, schedules for my-worker, R2 buckets and D1 database metadata."
#    Tools: {"resource":"capabilities"}, {"resource":"workers"},
#    {"resource":"worker_schedules","scriptName":"my-worker"}, {"resource":"r2_buckets"}.
# 8. "Set example.com's SSL mode to strict." Inspect zone_settings, then propose:
#    {"action":"update_zone_setting","zoneId":"bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb","settingId":"ssl","value":"strict"}
# 9. "Route example.com/api/* to my-worker." Inspect worker_routes, then propose:
#    {"action":"create_worker_route","zoneId":"bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb","pattern":"example.com/api/*","scriptName":"my-worker"}
# Unknown outcomes are never retried automatically; inspect Cloudflare first.

### Remove the token locally and disable; use current revision from GET
# Revoke the token separately in Cloudflare if it is no longer needed.
PUT {{origin}}/api/admin/workspaces/{{workspace}}/plugins/cloudflare
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "revision": 2,
  "settings": { "enabled": false, "authMethod": "api_token", "accountId": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", "zoneIds": ["bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb"] },
  "removeToken": true
}
